# CONFIG\MEMCFG - operator overrides for the memory map the BDS hands to
# the kernel. Install as CONFIG\MEMCFG in the efisp config container.
#
# NAME  BASE  SIZE  TYPE  ATTRIBUTE      (all five fields mandatory)
#   BASE/SIZE  hex, 4 KiB aligned
#   TYPE       UEFI memory type, number or name (CONVENTIONAL, RESERVED, ...)
#   ATTRIBUTE  EFI_MEMORY_* mask, hex; 0xF = UC|WC|WT|WB (normal RAM)
#
# Lines apply in order: a later line wins where it overlaps an earlier one.
# The table is a force - nothing is checked against TZ or the firmware.
#
# Total: ~318 MiB (235.6 modem block + 82.3 PIL gaps). Layout from the
# stock canoe vendor_boot DTB and the on-device UEFI map (PIL_Reserved is
# one UC-only RESERVED descriptor 0x8AA00000-0xA7CFFFFF).
#
# ---- modem block (235.6 MiB) ------------------------------------------
# A build that never starts the modem remoteproc has no use for the modem
# carveouts. Firmware marks these UC-only RESERVED (XBL label
# PIL_Reserved); the stock OS loads modem.mdt here, mainline has no
# qcom,kaanapali-mpss-pas node. UEFI itself loads nothing into this range
# (xbl_config pil: AutoStartImages=0, RetailImages=ABL,SPSS,ImageFv), so it
# is plain DDR at kernel entry.
#
# The kernel still honours its own device tree: with mpss_mem /
# q6_mpss_dtb / ipa_fw / ipa_gsi marked no-map in kaanapali.dtsi this gains
# nothing until those four nodes are removed there.
#
# ---- PIL gaps (82.3 MiB) ----------------------------------------------
# Holes inside PIL_Reserved that no reserved-memory node claims: alignment
# slack between the vendor carveouts plus the 25 MiB tail above adspslpi.
# The stock OS runs them as ordinary RAM; the UEFI map hides them inside
# the UC-only RESERVED descriptor, and the TZ merge deliberately never
# releases UC-only ranges - only this force table can. Kept regions stay
# untouched: gpu_microcode, camera/camera_2/cvp, video (iris), cdsp,
# spss+spu shared, dcp, soccp, adsp - anything a live remoteproc or
# firmware block may still own.
#
# Sizes and bases from the stock canoe vendor_boot DTB (reserved-memory
# nodes and the holes between them).

# modem block
mpss          0x8AA00000  0xEB00000  CONVENTIONAL  0xF
q6_mpss_dtb   0x99500000  0x80000    CONVENTIONAL  0xF
ipa_fw        0x99580000  0x10000    CONVENTIONAL  0xF
ipa_gsi       0x99590000  0xA000     CONVENTIONAL  0xF

# PIL gaps
pil_gap_ucode_cam    0x9959C000  0x64000    CONVENTIONAL  0xF
pil_gap_cdsp_spu     0x9CE80000  0x2E00000  CONVENTIONAL  0xF
pil_gap_spss_dcp     0x9FFE0000  0x70000    CONVENTIONAL  0xF
pil_gap_soccp_adsp   0xA0910000  0xA70000   CONVENTIONAL  0xF
pil_gap_adsp_tail    0xA6400000  0x1900000  CONVENTIONAL  0xF
